{"type":"standard","title":"Jim Desmond","displaytitle":"<span lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><span class=\"mw-page-title-main\">Jim Desmond</span></span>","namespace":{"id":0,"text":""},"wikibase_item":"Q16728515","titles":{"canonical":"Jim_Desmond","normalized":"Jim Desmond","display":"<span lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><span class=\"mw-page-title-main\">Jim Desmond</span></span>"},"pageid":29921701,"thumbnail":{"source":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6a/Jim_Desmond_Official_Portrait.jpg/330px-Jim_Desmond_Official_Portrait.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","width":330,"height":495},"originalimage":{"source":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/6/6a/Jim_Desmond_Official_Portrait.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","width":600,"height":900},"lang":"en","dir":"ltr","revision":"1370391806","tid":"4a192ed5-9cdf-11f1-84a1-d127319ca9d5","timestamp":"2026-08-20T21:37:06Z","description":"American politician","description_source":"local","content_urls":{"desktop":{"page":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jim_Desmond","revisions":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jim_Desmond?action=history","edit":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jim_Desmond?action=edit","talk":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Talk:Jim_Desmond"},"mobile":{"page":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jim_Desmond","revisions":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Special:History/Jim_Desmond","edit":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jim_Desmond?action=edit","talk":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Talk:Jim_Desmond"}},"extract":"Jim Desmond is an American politician and retired aviator serving as a member of the San Diego County Board of Supervisors since 2019, representing the fifth district. A member of the Republican Party, he previously served as vice chair of the board from 2020 to 2021, mayor of San Marcos, California from 2006 to 2018, and as a member of the San Marcos city council from 2004 to 2006.","extract_html":"<p><b>Jim Desmond</b> is an American politician and retired aviator serving as a member of the San Diego County Board of Supervisors since 2019, representing the fifth district. A member of the Republican Party, he previously served as vice chair of the board from 2020 to 2021, mayor of San Marcos, California from 2006 to 2018, and as a member of the San Marcos city council from 2004 to 2006.</p>"}